  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The temporal persistence with «solange»",
     "texto": [
      "1. **Temporal coextension**: «solange» establishes that the action of the main clause will remain in force for exactly the same period in which the subordinate situation continues: **Solange die Verhandlungen laufen, gilt der Waffenstillstand** (as long as negotiations are under way, the ceasefire applies).",
      "2. **Critical difference from «während» and «sobald»**: «Während» indicates a general temporal coincidence of two actions; «sobald» marks the immediate starting point; «solange» underlines the condition of parallel and indivisible duration.",
      "3. **Syntactic rule**: it always requires the conjugated verb at the end of the subordinate clause."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
